<resources>
    <string name="help_paper_title">📝 Paper Trading: pretend money, real prices</string>
    <string name="help_paper_body" formatted="false">Practise trading with pretend money at real prices; no real order goes anywhere. It opens from the 📝 button at the top or Menu → Paper Trading. The account starts with ₹10 lakh (start over from the Reckoning tab with anything from ₹1 lakh to ₹1 crore). In \"+ New order\" pick a stock, BUY or SELL, Intraday (MIS) or Delivery (CNC), and the order type: Market (at today\'s price), Limit (at your price or better), SL (on touching the trigger, up to the limit) or SL-M (on touching the trigger, at market). Give a stop-loss and target and the trade closes by itself at whichever comes first. Orders fill from Yahoo\'s 5-minute candles the way an exchange fills them: at the opening price on a gap, and only from candles after the order was placed. Intraday holds a fifth of the value as margin, can sell short, and is squared off by itself at 15:15; new intraday entries from 9:15 to 15:15. Delivery shares stay until sold. With the market closed an order fills at the next session\'s open (AMO); an order not filled during its day is cancelled at the close. Every trade pays real-looking charges: brokerage (intraday 0.03% or ₹20, delivery free), STT, exchange charges, SEBI fee, GST, stamp duty, and a DP charge when delivery shares are sold. While the section is open prices refresh every 30 seconds; with the app closed it checks every 15 minutes and notifies fills, stop-losses, targets and square-offs. The Reckoning tab shows wins and losses, profit factor, charges, the deepest fall, and trades from the app\'s plans against your own picks. In a stock\'s trade window, \"📝 Paper trade\" gives an order filled in at the plan\'s prices.</string>
